    "question": {
      ":question/id": "8b14da79-e96f-562a-85d5-426d65d14c7a",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "Find $(3\\mathbf{f}(t)-3\\mathbf{g}(t))^{\\prime}\\big|_{t=1}$, where $t>0$ and\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{f}(t)&=\\langle 2 e^{t - 1},\\,\\ln{\\left(t \\right)},\\,t^{2}\\rangle \\\\ \\mathbf{g}(t)&=\\langle -6,\\,- 2 t^{3},\\,2 \\sqrt{t}\\rangle\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Apply the **sum and constant multiple rules**:\n\n$$\n(3\\mathbf{f}(t)-3\\mathbf{g}(t))^{\\prime}=3\\mathbf{f}^{\\prime}(t)-3\\mathbf{g}^{\\prime}(t).\n$$\n\nDifferentiate each component:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{f}^{\\prime}(t)&=\\langle 2 e^{t - 1},\\,\\frac{1}{t},\\,2 t\\rangle \\\\ \\mathbf{g}^{\\prime}(t)&=\\langle 0,\\,- 6 t^{2},\\,\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{t}}\\rangle\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow evaluate the derivatives at $t=1$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{f}^{\\prime}(1)&=\\langle 2,\\,1,\\,2\\rangle \\\\ \\mathbf{g}^{\\prime}(1)&=\\langle 0,\\,-6,\\,1\\rangle\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nScale every component by its constant multiplier:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3\\mathbf{f}^{\\prime}(1)&=\\langle 6,\\,3,\\,6\\rangle \\\\ -3\\mathbf{g}^{\\prime}(1)&=\\langle 0,\\,18,\\,-3\\rangle\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdd corresponding components and combine like terms:\n\n$$\n(3\\mathbf{f}(t)-3\\mathbf{g}(t))^{\\prime}\\big|_{t=1}=\\langle 6,\\,21,\\,3\\rangle.\n$$\n\nKeep the displayed inner arguments when applying the scalar derivative rules; any nonunit inner derivative multiplies its component.",
