    "question": {
      ":question/id": "773d8137-1c81-5210-b56c-2e4a392e1126",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "Find $(\\mathbf{f}(t)-2\\mathbf{g}(t))^{\\prime}\\big|_{t=0}$, where $-1<t<\\frac{\\pi}{2}$ and\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{f}(t)&=\\langle t^{3},\\,\\ln{\\left(t + 1 \\right)},\\,- 2 \\sqrt{t + 1}\\rangle \\\\ \\mathbf{g}(t)&=\\langle \\sin{\\left(t \\right)},\\,2 \\tan{\\left(t \\right)},\\,- \\frac{2}{3 t + 3}\\rangle\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Apply the **sum and constant multiple rules**:\n\n$$\n(\\mathbf{f}(t)-2\\mathbf{g}(t))^{\\prime}=\\mathbf{f}^{\\prime}(t)-2\\mathbf{g}^{\\prime}(t).\n$$\n\nDifferentiate each component:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{f}^{\\prime}(t)&=\\langle 3 t^{2},\\,\\frac{1}{t + 1},\\,- \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{t + 1}}\\rangle \\\\ \\mathbf{g}^{\\prime}(t)&=\\langle \\cos{\\left(t \\right)},\\,2 \\sec^{2}{\\left(t \\right)},\\,\\frac{6}{\\left(3 t + 3\\right)^{2}}\\rangle\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow evaluate the derivatives at $t=0$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{f}^{\\prime}(0)&=\\langle 0,\\,1,\\,-1\\rangle \\\\ \\mathbf{g}^{\\prime}(0)&=\\langle 1,\\,2,\\,\\frac{2}{3}\\rangle\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nScale every component by its constant multiplier:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1\\mathbf{f}^{\\prime}(0)&=\\langle 0,\\,1,\\,-1\\rangle \\\\ -2\\mathbf{g}^{\\prime}(0)&=\\langle -2,\\,-4,\\,- \\frac{4}{3}\\rangle\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdd corresponding components and combine like terms:\n\n$$\n(\\mathbf{f}(t)-2\\mathbf{g}(t))^{\\prime}\\big|_{t=0}=\\langle -2,\\,-3,\\,- \\frac{7}{3}\\rangle.\n$$\n\nKeep the displayed inner arguments when applying the scalar derivative rules; any nonunit inner derivative multiplies its component.",
